<title>MOROCCO: Morocco calls bypass study tender.</title>
<headline>Morocco calls bypass study tender.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco on Thursday called for international tenders for a bypass of 560 kms (350 miles) linking the northern city of Tangier to Saidia on the Algerian-Moroccan frontier, the Public Works Ministry said.</p>
<p>It said it bidders to submit studies on the bypass could be Moroccan or foreign but any group should include at least one licensed Moroccan research bureau as part of their offer.</p>
<p>Offers close December 9, 1996.</p>
<p>The ministry said that about 300 kms (185 miles) of the bypass was already built but needed improving, while the remainder would be new construction.</p>
</text>
